# trios-mcp-rag — safe environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values locally. Never commit
# `.env`, and never substitute a real DSN, password, or token into THIS
# file. See:
#   - docs/rag/CANONICAL_PIPELINE.md  (anchor: TRIOS_PHD_SECRET_SAFETY)
#   - docs/agent-rules/03-safety-railway-postgres.md
#
# All values below are PLACEHOLDERS. Replace them with secrets stored in
# your local environment, a secrets manager, or your Railway "Variables"
# tab — never inline a real value here or anywhere in this repo.
#
# Postgres / Railway SSOT
# -----------------------
# The MCP server, the `build_pdf` MCP tool, and the `trios-mcp-rag
# build-pdf` CLI all read the DSN by environment variable name only.
# The DSN value is never printed, logged, written to a build artefact,
# or committed.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DBNAME

# Fallback DSN consulted by the pipeline when DATABASE_URL is unset.
# Same placeholder discipline applies.
RAILWAY_SSOT_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DBNAME

# Optional: which env-var name to consult. Leave commented unless you
# need to override (e.g. for a non-prod mirror).
# TRIOS_DATABASE_URL_ENV=DATABASE_URL

# Optional: which SSOT table to read from. The default is
# `ssot_brochure.chapters`; the accepted fallback is `ssot.chapters`.
# TRIOS_CHAPTERS_TABLE=ssot_brochure.chapters
